# Commit policy for AI assistants (Debt-Optimizer-Pro)

## Commit authorization

AI must NOT run `git commit`, `git push`, `git revert`, `git reset --hard`,
`git rebase`, or any other history-changing operation without an explicit
instruction from the user.

Direct triggers that authorize a commit:
- UA: «зроби коміт», «комить», «робимо коміт», «коміт».
- EN: «commit», «do the commit», «please commit».

If the message is ambiguous (`готово`, `ок`, `гаразд`, `ready`, `done`),
the AI MUST ask for confirmation via `AskQuestion` before committing.

## Local verification before every commit

Before committing, the AI MUST present a short pre-commit checklist with
concrete commands relevant to the changed scope, and either run what it
can or ask the user to run them.

Baseline checks for this monorepo:
- `pnpm --filter @workspace/aprly run typecheck` — frontend changes.
- `pnpm --filter @workspace/api-server run typecheck` — backend changes.
- `pnpm run typecheck` — `lib/*` or cross-package changes.
- IDE lints via `ReadLints` — any TS/TSX edit.
- `pnpm --filter @workspace/aprly run dev` — UI/visual changes (manual).
- `git diff --stat` summary of staged files.

The AI proceeds to commit only after the user confirms the checks passed.

## Commit message format

Authoritative regex (also enforced by the `commit-msg` hook from
`local_docs/commit_validate.txt`):

```regex
^(feat|fix|docs|style|refactor|test|chore):\s\[([A-Z]+-[0-9]+(,\s*)?)+\]\s.+$
```

Format: `<type>: [TICKET-ID] description`

- Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`.
- `TICKET-ID` MUST be a real Jira key obtained from the user (e.g. `[APRLY-12]`).
  The AI MUST request the key via `AskQuestion` before committing — never invent one.
- Multiple keys allowed via comma: `[APRLY-12, APRLY-13]`.
- Subject under 72 chars; optional body separated by a blank line.
- The hook regex accepts only `LETTERS-DIGITS` keys; complex Jira IDs like
  `[APR-SP1-E01-S03-T01]` will be rejected — use the canonical `[APRLY-N]` form.

### Examples

Correct:
- `feat: [APRLY-12] add landing optimizer wizard`
- `fix: [APRLY-34, APRLY-35] guard summary fields against null`

Incorrect:
- `feat: add landing` — missing ticket and brackets.
- `feat: [APR-SP1-E01-S03] ...` — non-canonical id, regex will reject.
- `update stuff` — missing type.

## Forbidden

- Editing `git config` (any scope).
- Using `--no-verify`, `--no-gpg-sign`, or any flag that bypasses hooks.
- Force-pushing to `main` or `petrychenko_dev` without explicit user request.
- Amending or rewriting commits authored by other contributors.
- Committing files that may contain secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens).

